    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** leading the charge at a commanding 72.58. His matchup against Trevor Rogers provides a rare combination of favorable platoon splits and a neutral park, boosting his efficiency significantly. Close behind, **Jackson Merrill** (66.99) and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (65.08) represent our high-floor anchors. **Jackson Merrill** benefits from a strong wind blowing out at his venue, which offsets a tougher matchup against Logan Webb, while **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** draws a favorable platoon look against a right-handed starter, pushing his score well into the elite tier of today's recommendations.\n\nTactical maneuvering was required to optimize our outfield depth, with **Sam Antonacci** (60.28) and **Wade Meckler** (59.97) edging out lower-ranked alternatives due to their leadoff and top-of-the-order roles. **Henry Bolte** (53.91) remains a volatile but necessary start thanks to an elite park environment that keeps him above our replacement threshold. The closest decision on the bench involved **Tommy White**, who registered a 46.26 score. While his park factors are stellar against Bryce Miller, his presumed placement at the bottom of the order and the lack of a platoon advantage relegated him to the pine behind more efficient high-volume producers.\n\nWe are monitoring several \"Lineup Pending\" statuses, specifically for **Josh Jung**, **Jackson Merrill**, and **Henry Bolte**; should any of these players move down in the order, their efficiency scores will require re-evaluation. Additionally, while **Gunnar Henderson** holds a respectable 61.97, owners should be wary of the matchup against Dylan Cease, whose elite stuff acts as a drag on the raw projection. We are maintaining discipline by benching **Coby Mayo** (38.79) and **Luis Lara** (36.14), as both failed to clear the 40.0 floor required to justify a start in our cap-sensitive format. Meanwhile, **Andy Pages** remains sidelined, and we will continue to monitor the statuses of **Luis Robert Jr.**, **Jordan Westburg**, **Jacob Wilson**, **Nasim Nunez**, **Heliot Ramos**, **Curtis Mead**, **Franklin Arias**, **Dominic Smith**, and **Liam Hicks** for future rotation spots.",
